       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Higher doses mostly add peripheral edema and hypotension rather than more blood pressure control.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you want:\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose. I can enter this now.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, if you want to start lower or titrate.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if it's intentional. I'd enter it with a note that you confirmed a dose above the usual maximum. Tell me if you'd like specific wording for the note.\n\nIf you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, you could add an agent from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide. I can enter that order too."
